ImagePullPolicy
===============
The ImagePullPolicy for a container and tag of image affect when kubelet attemps to pull the specified image.

IfNotPresent
The Image is pulled only when image is not already present locally.

Default ImagePullPolicy will be automatically set to IfNotPresent.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: java-pod
  namespace: production
  labels:
    application: java
spec:
  containers:
  - name: java-container
    image: mithuntechnologies/springboot-mongo-application:1
    imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
    ports:
    - containerPort: 8080

Always
Everytime while creating a container, kubectl will pull docker image.

It is recommended to set imagePullPolicy to Always.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: java-pod
  namespace: production
  labels:
    application: java
spec:
  containers:
  - name: java-container
    image: mithuntechnologies/springboot-mongo-application:1
    imagePullPolicy: Always
    ports:
    - containerPort: 8080

Never
Kubelet doesn't pull the Image.
When the Image is already present locally then kubelet attemps to start the container otherwise POD will not start.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: java-pod
  namespace: production
  labels:
    application: java
spec:
  containers:
  - name: java-container
    image: grafana/grafana
    imagePullPolicy: Never
    ports:
    - containerPort: 8080

